<article class="env-remark" id="0A1I">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A1I">Remark <span data-tag="0A1I">36.30.2</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $X$ be a scheme of finite presentation over $R$. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a finitely presented $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module flat over $R$ with support proper over $R$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0A1H" data-tag="0A1H">36.30.1</a> there exists a finite complex of finite projective $R$-modules $M^\bullet $ such that we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  R\Gamma (X_{R'}, \mathcal{G}_{R'}) = M^\bullet \otimes _ R R'  \]
</div>
  <p> functorially in the $R$-algebra $R'$. </p>
</article>